      "worked": "<strong>Rewrite 1 — wordy to concise</strong><br><strong>Before:</strong> 'Due to the fact that the server was not working in a proper manner, we were not able to make a decision regarding the launch at this point in time.' (31 words)<br><strong>After:</strong> 'Because the server was faulty, we could not decide about the launch now.' (13 words)<br><em>What changed:</em> 'due to the fact that' → 'because' · 'not working in a proper manner' → 'faulty' · 'were not able to' → 'could not' · 'make a decision regarding' → 'decide about' · 'at this point in time' → 'now'. Same meaning, 18 words saved.<br><br><strong>Rewrite 2 — passive to active</strong><br><strong>Before:</strong> 'The report was submitted by the team on Monday and it was approved by the manager on Tuesday.' (18 words)<br><strong>After:</strong> 'The team submitted the report on Monday. The manager approved it on Tuesday.' (13 words)<br><em>What changed:</em> both clauses flipped to active, and one long sentence split into two. Now each sentence carries one idea and names who did what.<br><br><strong>Rewrite 3 — one idea per sentence</strong><br><strong>Before:</strong> 'The workshop will start at 10 AM and the venue is the seminar hall and students must bring their identity cards and registration is compulsory.' (25 words, four ideas in one sentence)<br><strong>After:</strong> 'The workshop will start at 10 AM in the seminar hall. Registration is compulsory. Please bring your identity card.' (19 words, three clean sentences)<br><em>What changed:</em> every 'and' that joined two complete ideas became a full stop.",
