      "realLife": "Every abstract at the top of a research paper is a précis. So is the two-line summary your project guide asks for after you have spent an hour explaining your idea.",
      "worked": "<strong>Original passage (103 words):</strong><br>'Many students believe that reading a chapter once is enough to remember it. In reality, the human memory forgets most new information within a few days unless that information is used again. Teachers therefore advise students to revise a topic on the same day they learn it, again after one week, and once more before the examination. This method is called spaced revision. It does not require extra hours of study; it only requires that the same hours be spread out instead of being spent all at once. Students who follow it usually remember more and feel far less anxious before their examinations.'<br><br><strong>Step 1 — Central idea:</strong> One reading is not enough; revision spread over time works better.<br><strong>Step 2 — Main points underlined:</strong> (a) one reading is not enough (b) memory fades unless information is reused (c) revise same day, after a week, before the exam (d) this is called spaced revision (e) it needs no extra hours, only better spacing (f) it improves memory and reduces anxiety.<br><strong>Step 3 — Target length:</strong> 103 ÷ 3 ≈ 34 words. Aim for about 35 to 38.<br><strong>Step 4 — Cut:</strong> the phrase 'Many students believe' (opinion framing), 'It does not require extra hours of study; it only requires…' (compress to one clause), 'far less anxious before their examinations' (compress).<br><br><strong>TITLE: Spaced Revision</strong><br><strong>Précis (37 words):</strong> 'One reading is not enough, because memory fades unless information is reused. Teachers advise spaced revision — the same day, after a week, and before the examination. Requiring no extra hours, it improves memory and reduces examination anxiety.'<br><br><strong>Check the rules:</strong> Title ✅ · Own words ✅ · Third person ✅ · One paragraph ✅ · No new ideas ✅ · 37 of 103 words, close to one-third ✅ · All six main points present ✅",
