      "examAnswer": "A précis is a brief, clear and coherent summary of a passage, written in the summariser's own words, and reduced to approximately one-third of the original length. The procedure consists of reading the passage twice to grasp its sense, identifying the central idea and underlining the main points, calculating the target word count, preparing a rough draft from the underlined points, revising it for length and clarity, supplying a suitable title, and writing the fair copy with the word count stated. A précis must be written in the third person and generally in the past tense, must preserve the original order of ideas, must exclude examples, illustrations, repetitions and direct speech, and must not contain any new idea, comment or personal opinion of the writer.",
